  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project &quot;Get Your Hands Dirty&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FIB will conduct four workshops on its training for women, directed at representatives of civil society, government and businesses in the state of Rio de Janeiro; will develop an online database to improve its graduates&apos; employment rate with construction companies; and will produce a publication on its Projeto Mo na Massa. FIB will also extend its Projeto Mo na Massa, a six-month course in construction skills, to 160 women from favelas in Rio de Janeiro, whom it will train to become professional masons, carpenters, electricians and plumbers. The workers and their 300 family members will directly benefit; another 900 Brazilians will benefit from the practicum during which trainees expand or renovate an existing structure. (BR-855)</narrative>
  </description>
